+// RegisterSubmoduleIncludes (submodule include-path auto-discovery) removed:
+// it called DiscoverSubmodules(), which only exists in src/submodule_scanner.cpp
+// - a file CMakeLists.txt never adds to the `logicmake` executable's sources,
+// and nothing declares DiscoverSubmodules/SubmoduleInfo in a header main.cpp
+// includes. RegisterSubmoduleIncludes itself was never called from anywhere
+// in this file either, so this was dead code on both ends: unreachable, and
+// (until the fs:: alias got fixed) not even compilable. If the
+// submodule-include-discovery feature is still wanted, it needs
+// submodule_scanner.cpp added to CMakeLists.txt's source list and a shared
+// header declaring DiscoverSubmodules/SubmoduleInfo for main.cpp to call
+// into - that's a real feature to wire in deliberately, not something to
+// silently resurrect here.
